========================================================================================================
# The Python Standard Library (Built-In)
========================================================================================================
os: Interacts with the operating system file paths and directories.
math: Provides core mathematical functions and constants.
datetime: Handles dates, times, timezones, and time intervals.
json: Encodes and decodes JSON formatted data.
re: Executes regular expressions for advanced pattern matching.
collections: Extends built-in container types like lists and dictionaries.
urllib: Manages URL handling and basic web requests.
tkinter: Builds basic native desktop graphic user interfaces (GUIs)
========================================================================================================
# Data Science & Mathematics
========================================================================================================
NumPy: Handles efficient multi-dimensional array calculations and core linear algebra.
Pandas: Offers high-performance data manipulation via DataFrames.
SciPy: Extends NumPy with tools for advanced integration, optimization, and signal processing.
Polars: Executes blazingly fast data manipulation built on Rust.
SymPy: Performs symbolic mathematics, algebraic evaluation, and calculus.
========================================================================================================
# Machine Learning & Artificial Intelligence
========================================================================================================
Scikit-learn: Provides tools for classification, regression, and data clustering.
TensorFlow: Acts as a comprehensive infrastructure framework for deep learning models.
PyTorch: Delivers a dynamic framework optimized for deep neural network research.
Keras: Offers a streamlined, high-level interface for neural network layers.
XGBoost: Employs optimized gradient boosting algorithms for tabular data predictions.
Hugging Face Transformers: Houses pre-trained models for state-of-the-art Natural Language Processing (NLP).
========================================================================================================
# Data Visualization
========================================================================================================
Matplotlib: Serves as the foundational tool for building static or interactive charts.
Seaborn: Builds beautiful, high-level statistical graphics on top of Matplotlib.
Plotly: Generates highly interactive, web-ready graphs and complex dashboards.
Bokeh: Creates interactive, browser-based visual displays for enormous datasets.
========================================================================================================
# Web Development & Web Scraping
========================================================================================================
Django: Acts as a full-featured "batteries-included" backend web framework.
Flask: Serves as a lightweight micro-framework optimized for simple web apps.
FastAPI: Builds high-performance, asynchronous APIs with automatic documentation.
Requests: Sends user-friendly HTTP web requests seamlessly.
Beautiful Soup: Parses structured data out of HTML and XML source code.
Scrapy: Runs scalable web crawlers to systematically extract automated web data.
========================================================================================================
# Desktop GUIs, Games, & Computer Vision
========================================================================================================
: Provides extensive tools for crafting professional, native-looking desktop applications.
PyGame: Supplies graphic and audio controls for developing 2D multimedia games.
OpenCV: Drives advanced computer vision applications and real-time image processing.
Streamlit: Turns data analysis scripts into shareable web apps instantly.
